Props stands for Properties.
Props are arguments passed into React components.
It allow you to pass data from one component to another component.
Props are used to pass data from a parent component to a child component.
Props are passed to components via HTML attributes.
Props are read-only → Child cannot modify the Props because they are immutable.


Parent Component
      |
      |  passes data
      ↓
Child Component


PROPS
  ↓
Parent sends data/values
  ↓
Child receives data/values


